 "notes": "CASPEr-ZULF sideband search (Garcon et al.). Main result: Fig. 3, ALP wind-nucleon linear coupling g_aNN [GeV^-1], 90% CL, extracted from the vector boundary of the red excluded region in the e-print file Fig3-Exclusion-Linear.pdf, calibrated against the axis tick labels (913 path points binned to 100 median points in log-log space; jagged sensitivity-loss spikes at 0.21, 1.69, 2.16 Hz are smoothed by the binning). The paper defines H_wind = g_aNN grad(a).I_N with g_aNN in GeV^-1 and assumes g_app = g_ann = g_aNN; converted to the canonical dimensionless coupling via the 2m_N rule, g_an = 2 x 0.93957 GeV x g_aNN, reported as a neutron coupling with the (equal) proton coupling not separately reported. Plotted g_aNN runs from 4.6e-5 at 1.86e-16 eV to the top of the plot frame (1e-2) near 4.0-4.5e-14 eV; the last few points are clipped at the frame top, and the paper's stated bandwidth extends slightly further to 7.85e-14 eV (19 Hz) beyond the plotted axis. rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed (Eq. 2). The quadratic-wind (Fig. 4) and dark-photon (Fig. 5) limits from the same data are not reported here.",
